I went through the same thing recently - ascending all of the classes I
mean.  I learned that Healers and Rogues are two of my favorite
classes.  I'm sorry I'd ignored them for so long now.

I killed a lot of healers before I figured this out.  But now I think
I've got them down.  Here are my pointers -

Always do the protection racket.  They're made for it.  Gnomes are
easiest by far.

Use your pet and keep it healed. Your pet will quickly advance to Large
this way.  Almost nothing can survive a large dog or cat in the mines
below DLVL 10.  Two is even better.

Once you get to >2800gp do the racket.

Stay very close to your pet at all times.  Get a whistle, bell or leaf
as soon as you can to keep it near.

Don't be afraid to use your extra healing potions and bless them if
possible.  Every time you get near 25% max HP drink one.  By the time
you drink all of your healing potions your max HP should be near double
what you started with.

Use the E-word liberally and play defensively.

The key point is your pet.  Two large pets is like having an armed
entourage.  Later, a magic whistle + polytrap = 1 invincible pet and a
bunch of dead shopkeepers, guards and aligned priests.

After you've done the racket it becomes a normal game.  For weapons,
the darts are a good distance weapon but I don't advance that skill.  I
advance dagger though and toss them like crazy.  I will pick up a mace
or short sword or scimitar and advance it to Basic for melee.
Meanwhile look for a staff and advance it to Expert in anticipation of
the Staff of Aes... whatever, I can never spell it.

Have fun!
